Description: btrfs subvolume detection for GRUB's os-prober on Soplos Linux
 Soplos installers put the root filesystem in a "@" btrfs subvolume.
 GRUB's own btrfs filesystem driver only exposes the volume's top level
 (subvolid 5) to os-prober, so update-grub never finds /etc on another,
 unmounted Soplos installation and silently leaves it out of the boot
 menu unless its disk happens to already be mounted.
 .
 This package adds two grub.d scripts that mount the right subvolume
 read-only around os-prober's own pass, and patches a bug in os-prober's
 stock GRUB probe that otherwise reimports broken memtest86+ entries
 from the other system's own grub.cfg.

